<title>EGYPT: Egypt buys 5,000 t crude kernel oil at $715 - trade.</title>
<headline>Egypt buys 5,000 t crude kernel oil at $715 - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's official Holding Company for Food Industries bought on Wednesday 5,000 tonnes of crude kernel or coconut oil at $715 C+F per tonne for delivery in the first half of December, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the firm bought the oil from Kouk of Singapore. Egypt also bought 45,000 tonnes of sunflower and/or soya bean oil for $535.85 and $537.5 per tonne.</p>
<p>-- Miral Fahmy +202 578 3290/91</p>
